{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"As of 2026-11-06, Rule 6c-11 requires written policies and procedures governing the construction of baskets and their acceptance. For **custom baskets**, they must set detailed parameters for construction and acceptance, establish a process reasonably designed to ensure each is in the ETF’s and shareholders’ best interests, identify the adviser personnel who review each one and their responsibilities, and provide for reasonable segregation of duties.\n\nA **custom basket** is either a non-representative selection of portfolio holdings or a representative basket that differs from the initial basket used that business day. A **non-standard order** is an operational or market term—not the Rule’s definition. The terms are not interchangeable: an order may be non-standard without its basket meeting the regulatory custom-basket definition.\n\nKeep records of baskets exchanged with authorized participants, including basket contents, cash balancing amounts, AP identity, each custom basket’s rationale, and compliance review. Retain required records five years, with the first two readily accessible. *(17 C.F.R. § 270.6c-11(a), (c)(3), (d).)*"}}
